<title>MEXICO: Confia announces shareholding restructure.</title>
<headline>Confia announces shareholding restructure.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican bank Banca Confia S.A. (Confia) said on Wednesday that as part of its shareholding restructuring program it would convert some A series to B series shares, and it also announced its merger with leasing firm Aba Renda S.A. de C.V.</p>
<p>Confia said in a statement to the Mexican stock exchnage it would convert 304,526,210 A series shares, whose owner is the company's majority shareholder, to B series shares.</p>
<p>Confia's shareholding capital would thus stand at 1.720 billion pesos, accounted for by 877,200,000 A series and 842,800,000 B series shares.</p>
<p>The bank added that a special assembly had approved its merger with Aba Renda, which will cease to exist.</p>
<p>((--Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9562))</p>
